      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "655f376d-af79-587f-afa3-fb3e43a3f800",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kamehameha III, Kauikeaouli\n- Places: Hawaiian Islands, Hawaii\n- Organizations: Kingdom of Hawaiʻi\n- Products: Hawaiian dollar coinage, one-cent copper penny\n- Topics: Hawaiian coinage, monarchy\n\nFacts:\n- Kamehameha III, born Kauikeaouli, lived from 1813 to December 15, 1854.\n- Kamehameha III was the King of Hawaii from 1825 to 1854.\n- In 1847, the Kingdom of Hawaiʻi, under King Kamehameha III, issued its first official coinage.\n- The first official coinage of the Kingdom of Hawaiʻi was a large one-cent copper penny.\n- The Kingdom of Hawaiʻi issued the one-cent copper penny to alleviate the chronic shortage of small denomination coins circulating in the Hawaiian Islands.",
